    "question": "In a classroom of 81 students, two-thirds are wearing striped shirts while the others are wearing checkered shirts. If there are 19 more students wearing shorts than checkered shirts, how many more students are wearing striped shirts than shorts?",
    "gold": "8",
    "answer": "81/3 = <<81/3=27>>27 students are wearing checkered shirts.\n27 x 2 = <<27*2=54>>54 students are wearing striped shirts.\n27 + 19 = <<27+19=46>>46 students are wearing shorts.\n54 - 46 = <<54-46=8>>8 more students are wearing striped shirts than shorts.\n#### 8"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the number of students wearing striped shirts and checkered shirts, and then find out how many more students are wearing striped shirts than shorts.\n\n1. **Calculate the number of students wearing striped shirts:**\n   The total number of students is 81, and two-thirds of them are wearing striped shirts.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of students wearing striped shirts} = \\frac{2}{3} \\times 81 = 54\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the number of students wearing checkered shirts:**\n   The rest of the students are wearing checkered shirts. Since two-thirds are wearing striped shirts, one-third must be wearing checkered shirts.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of students wearing checkered shirts} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 81 = 27\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the number of students wearing shorts:**\n   There are 19 more students wearing shorts than checkered shirts.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of students wearing shorts} = 27 + 19 = 46\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate how many more students are wearing striped shirts than shorts:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Difference} = 54 - 46 = 8\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of students wearing striped shirts is 8 more than the number of students wearing shorts. The final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{8}\n\\]",
